# ADV-17 (2026-08-22): the ERROR-RECOVERY MODEL of core §8.3, pinned.
#
# §8.3 stated recovery as OBSERVED behaviour until this fixture landed; the
# rule it now states — a line that reports an error performs none of its state
# effects, and every other line is unaffected — was reachable only by matching
# the reference engine. Five sections, one recovery clause each. None of the
# five had a fixture of its own: the classes were pinned only as side effects
# of files whose subject was something else, or not at all.

figdown 0.1 block
# §8.3.4, cascade 1: an abandoned declaration contributes NO model element, so
# a later reference to it is a SECOND error. This is §8.3's own worked example
# (the shape, then the endpoint) plus the same shape on `class`.
node a "A" shape=hexagon
node b "B"
edge a -> b
class c
node d "D" class=c

figdown 0.1 block
# §8.3.5: a failed `layout` line does not OPEN the zone and does not consume
# the single-valued slot — `node c "C"` below is therefore accepted (an engine
# that opened the zone anyway would report a second error here) and the second
# `layout` opens the zone rather than answering `duplicate layout line`.
#
# §8.3.6: after the zone IS open, a CONNECTOR meets the zone gate ahead of its
# option pass and every other directive meets it after — one error either way,
# but not the same one.
node a "A"
node b "B"
layout junk
node c "C"
layout
edge a -> b stroke=notacolor
node e "E" fill=notacolor

figdown 0.1 bitfield
# §8.3.3 and §8.3.5. Line by line: `numbering=` is a TOLERATED fault, so the
# region opens and `field "A" 8` lands in it; a reserved-`;` line is refused
# BEFORE dispatch, so the region stays open and `field "C" 16` lands in it too
# (which is why there is no `bitfield has no fields`); and the failed opener
# `bitfield y` CLOSES x's region while opening none of its own, which is what
# `field "D" 8` reports.
bitfield x "X" numbering=zzz
field "A" 8
field "B" 24;
field "C" 16
bitfield y "Y" numbering=lsb0 fill=notacolor
field "D" 8

figdown 0.1 table
# §8.3.6: `duplicate width` is reported and the value fault on the same line
# is swallowed — the POSITIONAL half of the precedence asymmetry.
table t "T"
| A | B |
|---|---|
| 1 | 2 |
width auto,90
width auto,12em

figdown 0.1 block
# §8.3.6, the other half. The option stage runs ahead of every check the
# directive makes on its own, so the colour beats `duplicate id "a"`; and
# `pin`'s own value check runs ahead of ITS duplicate check, so the point
# beats `duplicate pin for "a"`. The two read in opposite directions and the
# asymmetry is engine-backlog item 79.
node a "A"
node a "B" fill=notacolor
layout
pin a at=(1,2)
pin a at=zz
